# macOS
.DS_Store

# R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# Generated analysis outputs — regenerable from the bigWigs + peaks + annotation
# by run_MINUTE.R, so none are committed (the .rds are tens of MB each). Only
# MINUTE_3 can run off a committed handoff; every other stage re-reads bigWigs
# anyway, so tracking the .rds bought little and cost repo size.
#
# Ignore the whole tree and name the exceptions, rather than listing the
# generated subfolders. Listing them meant any NEW output location was tracked
# by default: that is how 23 MB of generated GAM output (GAM_REPORT.html,
# chromosomes/, igv/) got committed in d685ac8 and 7a4f9e0 and had to be
# untracked again. The hand-written .md at the top level are the only source of
# truth here, so they are the only exceptions.
ChIP/results/*
!ChIP/results/EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md
!ChIP/results/METHODS.md
!ChIP/results/COMPARTMENT_CUTOFFS.md
# alternate output trees from MINUTE_RESULTS=... sensitivity runs (regenerable)
ChIP/results_*/

# Large raw inputs — downloaded from Google Drive (see ChIP/README.md), never
# committed. Peaks (ChIP/data/peaks) ARE committed. Default download targets:
ChIP/data/bigwig/
ChIP/data/annotation/
# Belt-and-suspenders in case MINUTE_DATA points somewhere else in the tree:
bigwig/
*.bw
LINE.mm39.bed
SINE.mm39.bed
LTR.mm39.bed
TAD_boundaries_mm39.bed

# GAM raw data — ~7.7 GB of NPMI matrices, differential contacts and hotspot
# tracks, delivered from the GAM processing pipeline, never committed. Same rule
# as the ChIP bigWigs: large, externally produced, not regenerable from this repo.
GAM/NPMI_matrices/
GAM/Diff_contacts/
GAM/Hotspots/
# GAM analysis outputs — regenerable by run_GAM.R from the data above. Same
# deny-all-then-except rule as ChIP/results: everything is generated except the
# hand-written METHODS.md. In particular GAM_REPORT.html (make_report.R),
# chromosomes/*.md (GAM_7_Figures.R) and igv/* (export_igv.R, README and session
# XML included) are all written by code and must not be committed.
GAM/results/*
!GAM/results/METHODS.md
GAM/results_*/

# stray base-R plot device output
Rplots.pdf
